  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What holds",
      "items": [
        "The swap of PhoneServer.link is under a lock, and release() only clears the link it owns, so the old thread cannot drop phone B (wsserver.py 161–172).",
        "Phone A's page ignores code 4000 and does not reconnect (face.js 161)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Finding: a stale frame after takeover",
      "items": [
        "serve_ws checks link.open at the top of its loop, then blocks in read_frame; a frame read after the close still goes to server.on_text (wsserver.py 275–278).",
        "Bridge.text(raw) does not know which link sent it (bridge_node.py 98–109). A late imu or touch from A is published as B's; a late hello from A would overwrite B's model until B's hello arrives.",
        "Impact is small (one frame, during a takeover); the fix is to pass the link to on_text and drop messages whose link is not current."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence level",
      "items": [
        "Read from the code at d2b04ac; not reproduced. The contract check covers the takeover itself (a second MockPhone closes the first), not the late frame."
      ]
    }
  ]
